  softbus_esi.xml - EtherCAT Slave Information for the soft_bus simulator
  (ecmaster project, Phase 8 step 8.2).

  Describes exactly what soft_bus puts in its SII image (tools/soft_bus/
  esc_sii.h + esc_build_sii() in esc_core.c), default pdo_size 4:
    Vendor 0x00000499 (internal test placeholder, NOT an ETG-assigned ID),
    Product 0x00000001, Revision 0x00000001
    SM0 mailbox out 0x1000/128 ctrl 0x26, SM1 mailbox in 0x1080/128 ctrl 0x22
    SM2 outputs 0x1100/4 ctrl 0x64 (WD trigger), SM3 inputs 0x1108/4 ctrl 0x20
    RxPDO 0x1600 (SM2): 0x7000:01 32 bit   TxPDO 0x1A00 (SM3): 0x6000:01 32 bit
    Mailbox: CoE only; expedited + segmented upload, expedited download;
             no SDO Info, no Complete Access, no PDO assign/config objects
    DC: SYNC0 (AssignActivate 0x0300)
  Checked against the soft_bus SII image with tools/esi/esi_check.py.

  ConfigData = SII words 0..6 (the configuring tool computes the word-7 CRC).
  Word 0 low byte 0x80 = PDI SPI, as for the LAN9252 in Platform 1. The other
  config words are 0 because soft_bus has no PDI; BEFORE this file is used to
  write a real LAN9252 EEPROM (Phase 2.5), words 0-6 must be re-derived from the
  LAN9252 datasheet (ESC config 0x0141, PDI config 0x0150-0x0153, SYNC/latch
  config 0x0151) - see ke_hoach_ethercat_v2.md section 1.2.
-->
